{"input": {"name": "member_chat_survives_refresh_flood", "stakeholder": "Member Services ops manager (R1)", "config": {"token_capacity": 1000, "token_refill_per_sec": 100, "reserves": {"CRITICAL": 0.0, "STANDARD": 0.1, "DEFERRABLE": 0.4}}, "identities": {"chat-frontend": "member_chat", "claims-worker": "claims_summary", "refresh-job": "policy_refresh"}, "enforce": true, "steps": [{"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "refresh-job", "id": "r1", "token_estimate": 600}, {"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "refresh-job", "id": "r2", "token_estimate": 100}, {"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "claims-worker", "id": "c1", "token_estimate": 250}, {"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "claims-worker", "id": "c2", "token_estimate": 100}, {"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "chat-frontend", "id": "m1", "token_estimate": 150}]}, "output": {"results": [{"allowed": true, "reason": "admitted"}, {"allowed": false, "reason": "floor"}, {"allowed": true, "reason": "admitted"}, {"allowed": false, "reason": "floor"}, {"allowed": true, "reason": "admitted", "workload": "member_chat"}], "showback": {}}, "why": "The refresh takes 600 and must stop at its 400 floor (r2 shed). Claims takes 250 and must stop at its 100 floor (c2 shed). The 150 left belongs to members: a 150-token chat is admitted and takes the bucket to zero. Lower tiers cannot starve chat, and chat can spend what they were made to leave."}
{"input": {"name": "tier_comes_from_identity", "stakeholder": "CISO (R5)", "config": {"token_capacity": 1000, "token_refill_per_sec": 100, "reserves": {"CRITICAL": 0.0, "STANDARD": 0.1, "DEFERRABLE": 0.4}}, "identities": {"chat-frontend": "member_chat", "claims-worker": "claims_summary", "refresh-job": "policy_refresh"}, "enforce": true, "steps": [{"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "claims-worker", "id": "c1", "token_estimate": 300, "claimed_workload": "member_chat"}, {"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "laptop-script", "id": "x1", "token_estimate": 100}, {"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "chat-frontend", "id": "m1", "token_estimate": 100, "claimed_workload": "member_chat"}, {"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "claims-worker", "id": "c2", "token_estimate": 550, "claimed_workload": "member_chat"}]}, "output": {"results": [{"allowed": true, "reason": "admitted", "workload": "claims_summary", "spoof_attempt": true}, "PermissionError", {"allowed": true, "reason": "admitted", "workload": "member_chat", "spoof_attempt": false}, {"allowed": false, "reason": "floor", "workload": "claims_summary", "spoof_attempt": true}], "showback": {}}, "why": "The claims worker claims to be member chat. The claim is ignored and flagged, and the call is decided as claims. c2 shows why it matters: 550 from the 600 left would be admitted as CRITICAL but is shed as STANDARD (50 < 100 floor). An unknown caller is rejected outright, the escalate case: no identity, no tier, no guess."}
{"input": {"name": "shadow_mode_and_kill_switch", "stakeholder": "SRE lead (R7)", "config": {"token_capacity": 1000, "token_refill_per_sec": 100, "reserves": {"CRITICAL": 0.0, "STANDARD": 0.1, "DEFERRABLE": 0.4}}, "identities": {"chat-frontend": "member_chat", "claims-worker": "claims_summary", "refresh-job": "policy_refresh"}, "enforce": false, "steps": [{"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "refresh-job", "id": "r1", "token_estimate": 700}, {"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "chat-frontend", "id": "m1", "token_estimate": 900}, {"t": 0, "op": "set_enforce", "value": true}, {"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "refresh-job", "id": "r2", "token_estimate": 50}, {"t": 0, "op": "set_enforce", "value": false}, {"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "refresh-job", "id": "r3", "token_estimate": 50}]}, "output": {"results": [{"allowed": true, "reason": "floor", "enforced": false}, {"allowed": true, "reason": "admitted", "enforced": false}, null, {"allowed": false, "reason": "floor", "enforced": true}, null, {"allowed": true, "reason": "floor", "enforced": false}], "showback": {}}, "why": "Shadow mode never blocks: r1 runs but is recorded as a would-shed, and the policy's own bucket isn't charged for it, so m1 is judged against a full bucket. Enforcing blocks r2. Turning enforcement off again (the kill switch) restores today's behaviour mid-run: r3 runs and is recorded."}
{"input": {"name": "showback_charges_what_ran", "stakeholder": "FinOps lead (R10)", "config": {"token_capacity": 1000, "token_refill_per_sec": 100, "reserves": {"CRITICAL": 0.0, "STANDARD": 0.1, "DEFERRABLE": 0.4}}, "identities": {"chat-frontend": "member_chat", "claims-worker": "claims_summary", "refresh-job": "policy_refresh"}, "enforce": false, "steps": [{"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "refresh-job", "id": "r1", "token_estimate": 700}, {"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "chat-frontend", "id": "m1", "token_estimate": 300}, {"t": 0, "op": "settle", "id": "r1", "token_actual": 650}, {"t": 0, "op": "settle", "id": "m1", "token_actual": 240}, {"t": 0, "op": "settle", "id": "m1", "token_actual": 240}, {"t": 0, "op": "set_enforce", "value": true}, {"t": 0, "op": "submit", "caller": "refresh-job", "id": "r2", "token_estimate": 600}, {"t": 0, "op": "settle", "id": "r2", "token_actual": 600}]}, "output": {"results": [{"allowed": true, "reason": "floor"}, {"allowed": true, "reason": "admitted"}, null, null, "KeyError", null, {"allowed": false, "reason": "floor"}, "KeyError"], "showback": {"Content Operations": 650, "Member Services": 240}}, "why": "Finance pays for what ran. r1 was a would-shed but ran in shadow mode, so its 650 actual tokens are charged to Content Operations. m1 is charged 240, not its 300 estimate. Settling twice fails. r2 was blocked, never ran, can't be settled and costs nothing."}
{"input": {"name": "gate_stops_when_cheap_fix_suffices", "stakeholder": "Sponsor (R12)", "op": "gates", "thresholds": {"t_chat": 0.05, "m2_min": 0.5, "m3_min": 0.5, "m4_max_points": 15, "m6_p99_ms_max": 1.0, "m8_max": 0}, "metrics": {"m1_today": 0.19, "m2_backoffice_share": 0.9, "m1_option1": 0.04}}, "output": {"gates": {"G0": "PROCEED", "G1": "STOP", "G2": "NOT REACHED"}}, "why": "The problem is real (19% > 5%) and mostly caused by back-office load (90% \u2265 50%), so G0 proceeds. Moving the refresh alone brings chat failures to 4%, under the target, so G1 stops the gateway program. G2 is never evaluated. Stopping here is the correct, cheaper outcome, and the instrument must say so plainly."}
